@*
    Shared form-row primitive — the canonical, repo-wide building block for
    any form (create / edit / wizard step / dialog) that needs a horizontal
    label + input row.

    THE PATTERNS (School-Collab form layout convention, v4.14.2):

    HORIZONTAL (default — <FormRow Orientation="Horizontal">):

      ┌─ .form-row (display: flex, align-items: center, gap: 12px) ─────┐
      │ ┌─ .form-row-label (width: 180px, flex-shrink: 0) ──┐ ┌─ input ┐ │
      │ │ "Contact email *" (left, equal-width every row)    │ │  cell  │ │
      │ └────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘ └────────┘ │
      └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
        all labels: 180px      all input cells start at the SAME x
                               (label width + gap is a constant)

    VERTICAL (<FormRow Orientation="Vertical">):

      ┌─ .form-row (display: flex, flex-direction: column, gap: 4px) ──┐
      │ ┌─ .form-row-label (width: 100%) ──────────────────────────────┐ │
      │ │ "Contact email *" (TOP, full width)                            │ │
      │ └───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘ │
      │ ┌─ .form-row-input (width: 100%) ─────────────────────────────┐  │
      │ │  input cell                                                  │  │
      │ └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘  │
      └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

    Why two orientations:
      - Horizontal is the canonical layout. The LABEL column is the CONSTANT
        (fixed 180px on every row), so every label in a form has identical
        width and reads as a single uniform block down the form. The INPUT
        column is the VARIABLE (flex:1; min-width:0), so every input cell
        takes the remaining width and every input's left edge lands on the
        same vertical axis — inputs align down the form even when their
        individual intrinsic widths differ.
      - Vertical is for narrow surfaces (side drawers, mobile, etc.) where
        the 180px horizontal column would consume too much of the row. The
        label moves above its input cell, full width, and the input cell
        drops to a new line. Use explicitly via Orientation="Vertical" —
        do NOT rely on the responsive `@media (max-width: 720px)` fallback
        to "happen to" stack the row (that's only for genuine phone widths;
        a 420px drawer hosted in a desktop browser is below the viewport
        breakpoint and would unhelpfully inherit the stacked layout too).
      - align-items: center (default) keeps the label text on the same
        line as the input control on a horizontal row; a wrapping label
        still centers its first line. For vertical orientation this is
        moot (label sits on its own line above).
      - Plain <div> wrappers (not FluentStack) are intentional: they are
        the lightest layout primitive, keep CSS-isolation scope clean
        (the wrapper divs are authored here, so they receive THIS
        component's scope attribute and the rules below actually match).

    Usage (in a form component):
        <EditForm ...>
            <FormRow Label="Student number" Required For="studentFormNumber">
                <FluentTextField Id="studentFormNumber" @bind-Value="..." />
            </FormRow>
            <FormRow Label="Dates" AlignTop For="periodStart">
                <FluentDatePicker Id="periodStart" @bind-Value="..." />
                <FluentDatePicker Id="periodEnd"   @bind-Value="..." />
            </FormRow>
            <FormRow Label="Email" Orientation="Vertical" Required>
                <FluentTextField ... />
            </FormRow>
        </EditForm>

    Parameters:
      - Label       (required) the visible label text.
      - Required    optional, renders a red asterisk after the label.
      - For         optional, the DOM id of the input the <label> points to.
                    When null the <label> has no `for` attribute (still
                    rendered, just not clickable-to-focus).
      - LabelTip    optional, surfaces as a native title= tooltip on the label.
      - AlignTop    optional, top-aligns the row instead of centering. Use
                    for multi-input horizontal rows (e.g. two date pickers
                    side-by-side) where centering the label against a tall
                    cell looks off. Default false (center, the modern
                    default for single-input rows). No effect on Vertical.
      - Orientation optional, picks Horizontal (label left + input right,
                    the canonical repo layout) or Vertical (label top +
                    input below). Default Horizontal. Use Vertical for
                    narrow containers (side drawers, stacked mobile
                    layouts) where the 180px horizontal column would
                    consume too much of the row.
      - ChildContent (required) the input(s) for the row.
*@

<div class="form-row form-row--@(Orientation.ToString().ToLowerInvariant()) @(AlignTop ? "form-row--align-top" : null)">
    <div class="form-row-label">
        <label for="@For" title="@LabelTip">@Label @if (Required) { <span class="form-row-required" aria-hidden="true">*</span> }</label>
    </div>
    <div class="form-row-input">
        @ChildContent
    </div>
</div>

@code {
    /// <summary>Visible label text. Required.</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public string Label { get; set; } = default!;

    /// <summary>When true, renders a red asterisk after the label.</summary>
    [Parameter] public bool Required { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Optional DOM id of the input the <c>&lt;label&gt;</c> targets.</summary>
    [Parameter] public string? For { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Optional native tooltip on the label.</summary>
    [Parameter] public string? LabelTip { get; set; }

    /// <summary>
    /// Top-align the row instead of centering. Use for multi-input horizontal
    /// rows (e.g. two date pickers side-by-side) where centering the label
    /// against a tall cell looks off. Default false (center, the modern
    /// default for single-input rows). No effect when Orientation is Vertical.
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter] public bool AlignTop { get; set; }

    /// <summary>
    /// Row orientation. <see cref="RowOrientation.Horizontal"/> (default)
    /// renders the label on the left in the canonical 180px column with
    /// the input cell to its right. <see cref="RowOrientation.Vertical"/>
    /// stacks the label on top of the input cell, full width — use for
    /// narrow surfaces (side drawers, stacked mobile layouts) where the
    /// 180px horizontal column would consume too much of the row.
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter] public RowOrientation Orientation { get; set; } = RowOrientation.Horizontal;

    /// <summary>The input(s) for the row. Required.</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public RenderFragment ChildContent { get; set; } = default!;
}
